Z||000005||007DOUG||09-01-2000||09:25 AM||||"Sticks and stones may break my bones, but names will never harm me."<P>Am I the only person that understands this?<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BellaFiero||09-01-2000||10:21 AM||||We are a wicked lot. We all want to be driving our little exotics as if they WERE exotics, with Lamborghini badging or some such. Tell me who hasn’t brought up the “Lotus” suspension at ONE time in an effort to back their car’s “sport” image. Not a lot of people will give our cars that image, and those that do are usually not even aware that Fieros even existed. Most people who don’t own a Fiero, but were around when they were released, are not exactly enthusiastic about our little car. They give “sport’s car” titles to Vettes and Ram Air Trans Am ( hell, most people nowadays don’t even contribute the Mustangs and Firebirds to being sporty – rather just powerful luxury ). Don’t forget that there probably are a lot of kids on this page, and they have dreams. I know I do. Hell, folks, my car has a hood scoop on the HOOD. I justify by saying I’ve got it routed to the radiator – yeah, it blows air at the radiator. I’m sure that’s why I did it. NO. I did it because hood scoops intimidate the local gear heads and Ricers. And I always thought the Fiero’s body lines needed a scoop on the hood. Much more aggressive. But whatever. The point is, people are going to do things to their car that other people don’t like. And you’re going to have to deal with it. It will always happen. It’s my car – if someone one the forum doesn’t like the scoop or the neon or the neon-illuminating switches, the 10” bass box in the passenger seat or the one under the hood, or the custom sail panels or…. Well, whatever! If anyone here has a problem with any of that, PLEASE let me know you’re opinion. Maybe it is really silly, or maybe you want details on how to do it to YOUR car. But this is a place of opinions. Even when you claim to be stating facts. I remember when someone stated that the Tach on a four cylinder automatic would read 4,000 RPMs when you were doing eighty miles an hour. And I quote “ That’s A Fact” …. Bite ME! My car’s needle is buried to the last number in my odometer, and it still is a good half inch from 4,000. So take your fact and eat it. Anyone have a problem with that? Then come to my house and I’ll take you for a spin. And that’s the attitude we need. We are pretty much self-policed. We take care of our own, for the most part. But don’t get upset when some creep out there throws an insult. Remember, he’s hiding behind anonymity and distance. He doesn’t even have to say it to your face to insult you. So what does his opinion matter? Who cares? It’s your car – enjoy it. If someone else doesn’t, someone else who is States or Countries away, then that is THEIR problem. Twin Turbo? Yeah… hard to believe. Keep in mind that if you have something rare or ‘impossible’, you’re going to have to give us some proof. We’re not asking you to make us LIKE your car – just let us know it EXISTS. Sorry for the long post.||||reg||8
Z||000007||HugGRRRFiero||09-01-2000||11:04 AM||||Actually, this forum is the best one I've ever been to.  Nobody really rips into anyone unless they say something really funny, hehe (no flame intended) for example "My rear is sagging... Please Help" with "big crack in my rear" in the message.  I had to laugh at the immediate responses, but in the end I think the guy got the info he was looking for.<P>You just have to be careful with sarcasm, It's very easy to mis-interpret meanings from just text.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-01-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000008||BN Boomer||09-01-2000||11:42 AM||||Yeah, I have to agree with HugGRRR. This is probably one of the best behaved boards I've ever seen. For those of you who don't like being called out for posting BS, well, don't post BS! Imagine that!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||09-01-2000||11:54 AM||||Did I miss something again?  Usually Cliff just locks up the flame wars, but I didn't notice any new locked threads (I would have read 'em--kinda like reading the Nat'l Enquirerererer) or any flames lately.  (At least not since the original Archie thing.)  I thought we've been getting along fairly well lately.  Can't we all just get along?<P>Doug--I heard it a different way.  "Sticks and stones may break my bones, but whips and chains excite me."  (j/k <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||09-01-2000||01:36 PM||||It's not like anyone claimed to have a crashed flying saucer. A Twin Turbo Intercooled Yugo is possible. Consider what people will kludge together, it's even likely. TT NS? Maybe, maybe not.<P>At some point, you have to just keep quiet on extraordinary claims if they are beyond your beliefs. There is no way to call people on it without sounding *mean and nasty*. Just don't add to the thread. <P>Yes, I think there are some nearly unbelievable claims made, but 99.99999% of what's here is so damn good, it just don't call people on it.<P>As mom used to say, "If you can't say something good......".<P>&lt;End of transmission&gt;||||reg||1
Z||000011||GT Bastard||09-01-2000||01:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>Yeah, I have to agree with HugGRRR. This is probably one of the best behaved boards I've ever seen. For those of you who don't like being called out for posting BS, well, don't post BS! Imagine that!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Amen to that, brutha.  My sentiments exactly.  I think it's funny as hell to watch members flame each other on occasion.  Get it out of your system.  Just because you have an argument with another forum member, it doesn't mean you have to run away crying forever.  There have been plenty of forum members in the past that I thought were imbiciles at first, but I can now appreciate what they have to say.  I'm sure a good many feel the same about me.  If someone is genuinely upset, just cry.  You'll feel better afterwords.  And about the grammer police a.k.a GT Bastard, I only start that nonsense when the actual content of the post is "BS."  There's plenty of misspellings that go unpunished on this forum.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Bwahahahha....<P>BTW, if the occasional flame hurts your feelings, check out <A HREF="http://www.LS6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.LS6.com</A>  or just about any other forum.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000012||GT Bastard||09-01-2000||01:55 PM||||PS-  Stimpy, you crack me up!  Keep calling them like you see 'em.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DjKid||09-01-2000||02:01 PM||||I just wanted to add, no flaming, that 'stangs, TransAms, Camaros shouldn't be considered sporty, cuz they are not sports. they are muscle cars. Now perhaps 2003, when they both, camaro and 'stang, get thier redesign, they will have some more sporty features I'm sure, 4wheel disc, 4 wheel indepedent suspension, and the such. But they are MUSCLE cars! Not sports cars!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djkid_sig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>'Blue Knight'</A>||||reg||1
